      <manifestationList xml:id="sourceDesc_d8846d5e">
         <manifestation label="" xml:id="source_d1e33">
            <titleStmt xml:id="titleStmt_80e804b1">
               <title xml:id="title_164N2004A">Score, autograph, fair copy</title>
            </titleStmt>
            <physDesc xml:id="physDesc_48231836">
               <extent xml:id="extent_93c627c9">8 pages</extent>
               <dimensions unit="cm" xml:id="dimensions_f5095db6">34.5 x 26</dimensions>
               <physMedium xml:id="physMedium_6a673e5c">2 bifolios. Written in purple and black ink. Paper: fol. 1: 16 staves; fol. 2: 12 staves. Title at the bottom of the page: "Thema med 14 Variationer, skrevne for Johan Peter Hartmann / Nærum 5/8 81 / JPEH." (Theme with 14 Variations, Written for Johan Peter Hartmann). Johan Peter was Hartmann's eight-year old grandson. On a couple of empty staves the latter has practiced the notation of scales in pencil. On p. 2 a two-part piece without title, crossed out, apparently also intended for use in a pedagogical context. (HartW 124). The two bifolios have been cut apart and glued together again in a new way, thereby changing the order of the variations. Furthermore, some of the original numbers of the variations have been crossed out and new numbers added in pencil.</physMedium>
            </physDesc>
